White Noise and Forecasting
Trend Data
100, 120, 140, 160, 180

Easy to forecast because there is a pattern.

White Noise
100, 95, 108, 97, 103, 99, 106

No pattern.

Forecasting models cannot learn anything useful.

=========


Relation to ARIMA

When building an ARIMA model:

Convert data to stationary.
Train the model.
Check the residuals (errors).

If residuals look like White Noise:

✅ Good model

Why?

Because the model has already captured all meaningful patterns, leaving only random noise.

Interview Answer

White Noise is a completely random stationary time series with no trend, seasonality, or predictable pattern. 
Since past values do not help predict future values, White Noise cannot be used for forecasting.
In time series modeling, residuals should ideally resemble White Noise after fitting a good model.
